userStories.description:
**Goal** — Command-caused degraded run-start baseline markers and their logs retain bounded, redacted evidence.

**Motivation** — A 3m42s root capture written as `unparseable` left no way to tell a phase cap from a crash or a real failure.

**Approach** — **Evidence on degraded markers (`test-baseline-capture.ts`, `verification/test-baseline.ts`).** The `no-baseline` arm of `TestBaseline` gains `evidence?: BaselineEvidence`:

```ts
export interface BaselineEvidence {
  readonly command: string;
  readonly cwd: string;
  readonly exitCode?: number;
  readonly durationMs: number;
  readonly outputTail?: string;
  readonly error?: string;
}
```

The capture loop records, per command it runs, the command, its cwd, its own duration, and its result. The duration comes from a new `_captureDeps.clockMs: () => number` (production `Date.now`), read exactly twice per command, immediately before and after `runCommand`; the existing `durationMs` on the `Run-start test baseline captured` line keeps using `Date.now` as today. When it writes a degraded marker caused by a command, the marker carries that command's evidence: for `timeout` the command that timed out; for `error` from a runner throw the command that threw, with `error` set from `errorMessage(err)` and no `outputTail`; for `unparseable` the first command in run order whose result was not `success`. `test-baseline.json` is committed to the repo, so every evidence field is safe to persist: `command` and `error` pass through `redactSecrets` (`@/logger`); `cwd` is stored relative to the capture `root` (`"."` for the root itself); `outputTail` is the command output passed through `gateOutputTail` (redacts secrets, then keeps the last 40 lines of at most 500 characters each) and is omitted when the output is empty. `exitCode` is present only when the runner reported one. The `No run-start test baseline` info line spreads the same fields after `reason`. Markers not caused by a command (`gate-disabled`, `no-test-command`, and `error` from the outer catch) carry no `evidence` and log `{ reason }` as today.

`gateOutputTail` lives in `src/operations/gate-output-tail.ts` and is in no barrel. `src/operations/full-suite-gate.ts:24` documents that `operations` already imports from `execution`, so importing the `@/operations` barrel from `execution` risks a cycle under `check:import-cycles`. The file therefore moves to its own nested barrel `src/operations/gate-output-tail/index.ts` with unchanged exports; the capture imports `@/operations/gate-output-tail` (an exact nested-barrel alias, which `check:alias-internals` allows), and the existing `./gate-output-tail` imports in `lint-check.ts` and `typecheck-check.ts` resolve to the directory unchanged.

**Scope** — In: additive evidence type, per-command clock seam, sanitized marker/log evidence, helper relocation and focused evidence tests. Out: US-001's no-pending capture guard and git refusals; US-003's resolver and package baseline selector; US-004's capture units/grouping; US-005's totals. The `no-baseline` reasons and the run-level degraded semantics (any timeout or throw degrades the whole baseline) are not changed to per-package outcomes. A phase that exceeds its cap in `run-tests.ts` still yields no test names; the baseline for it stays `unparseable`, now with evidence.

**Interface** — `TestBaseline` no-baseline arm gains `evidence?: BaselineEvidence`; `TestBaselineCaptureDeps` and `_captureDeps` gain `clockMs: () => number`. `writeNoBaseline(root, featureId, reason)` takes an optional `BaselineEvidence`, persists it on the marker and spreads it into the log line. `gateOutputTail(output: string): string` and its constants retain their exports from the nested barrel.

**Integration and tests** — Create `packages/nax/test/unit/execution/lifecycle/test-baseline-capture-evidence.test.ts` because `test-baseline-capture.test.ts` is at 770 of 800 lines. The `test.each` `logs no-baseline reason` in `test-baseline-capture-logging.test.ts` asserts `data: { reason }` exactly for every reason; the `timeout`, `unparseable` and runner-throw `error` rows run a command, so their log data now also carries `command`, `cwd` and `durationMs`; those three rows assert `data` with `expect.objectContaining({ reason })`, and the `gate-disabled` and `no-test-command` rows keep the exact `data: { reason }`. Preserve root command-list aggregation, the fail-open outer catch and green-capture logging. Use `_captureDeps` with restored snapshots and independently assert secret redaction in command, error and output.

**Goal** — Share test command/cwd resolution between consumers and restrict test gate attribution to the story's own package coverage.

**Motivation** — Meanwhile the per-story test gate (`_fullSuiteGateDeps.resolveGateContext`, `full-suite-gate.ts:154`) resolves the story package's command from the package-merged config and runs it per `resolveGateCwd`, unprefixed. The baseline and the gate measure different commands.

**Approach** — **Shared suite-command resolver (`operations/suite-test-command/index.ts`, `operations/full-suite-gate.ts`).** The command and cwd logic of `_fullSuiteGateDeps.resolveGateContext` moves into a new nested barrel so the per-package capture and the gate can never resolve different commands:

```ts
// packages/nax/src/operations/suite-test-command/index.ts
export interface SuiteTestCommand {
  readonly testCmd: QualityCommandSpec;   // string | string[]
  readonly cmdWorkdir: string;
  readonly provenance: GateCommandProvenance;
}
export async function resolveSuiteTestCommand(input: {
  readonly packageView: PackageView;
  readonly workdir: string;       // absolute package dir
  readonly packageDir?: string;   // storyPackageDir(story); undefined at the repo root
}): Promise<SuiteTestCommand | undefined>;
```

It runs `resolveQualityTestCommands(packageView.config, workdir, packageDir)`; when no command resolves, the detection fallback `resolveDefaultQualityCommands(workdir).test` with `cmdWorkdir = workdir` and provenance `"detected"`; otherwise `resolveGateCwd({ commandName: "test", detected: false, packageView, workdir })`. It returns `undefined` when neither yields a command. `resolveGateContext` calls it and keeps throwing `TEST_COMMAND_MISSING` on `undefined` with its current message and context. The one visible difference: the detected-command branch, which today returns no `cmdProvenance`, now returns `cmdProvenance: "detected"`, so the gate's log line carries it. The module imports nothing from `src/execution/`.

**Match gate findings against their own package (`verification/test-baseline.ts`, `operations/full-suite-gate.ts`).** `BaselineEntry` gains `packageDir?: string` and the captured arm of `TestBaseline` gains `packageDirs?: string[]`. A new pure `baselineForPackage(baseline: TestBaseline | undefined, packageDir: string): TestBaseline | undefined` returns its input unchanged when it is `undefined`, a `no-baseline`, or a captured baseline with no `packageDirs`; returns `undefined` when `packageDirs` does not include `packageDir`; and otherwise returns a new captured baseline whose `entries` are those with `(entry.packageDir ?? ".") === packageDir`. `labelFindingsWithBaseline` applies it, with `packageDir = storyPackageDir(input.story) ?? "."`, to both the resolved story baseline and the run baseline before `applyBaselineDispositions`. `applyBaselineDispositions` and `matchEntry` are unchanged; an `undefined` story baseline already yields `unattributed`.

**Scope** — In: nested command resolver, gate delegation/provenance, additive package metadata, pure package selector and gate labeling wiring. Out: US-004 captures per-package units and writes that metadata; US-002 adds evidence and relocates gateOutputTail; US-001 guards capture and diagnoses HEAD movement; US-005 totals phase output. Per-story roll-forward baselines (`writeStoryBaseline`, `source: "roll-forward"`) are not written or changed. `applyBaselineDispositions`, `matchEntry` and the disposition values are not changed.

**Interface** — Use the SuiteTestCommand and resolveSuiteTestCommand declarations above; additionally `baselineForPackage(baseline: TestBaseline | undefined, packageDir: string): TestBaseline | undefined`, `BaselineEntry.packageDir?: string`, and captured `TestBaseline.packageDirs?: string[]`. The `_fullSuiteGateDeps.resolveGateContext` seam and FullSuiteGateContext remain compatible, with detected `cmdProvenance` now populated.

**Integration and tests** — Existing baseline tests build entries and baselines without the new optional fields. Create `packages/nax/test/unit/operations/suite-test-command.test.ts` and `packages/nax/test/unit/verification/test-baseline-package.test.ts`; extend existing full-suite-gate and quality-gate-packageview fixtures to prove real gate wiring and missing-command errors. US-003 creates `resolveSuiteTestCommand`; the gate-op AC with the stubbed resolver pins the gate call site, and US-004's production `resolveUnit` AC pins the capture call site. US-003 creates `baselineForPackage`; the two gate-op ACs labelling the same failure `introduced` in `packages/b` and `pre-existing` in `packages/a` pin its wiring. Preserve the root/overlay/detected cwd rules, review-command precedence, array commands and fallback detection; never reimplement quality command resolution.
